  "live_records": {
    "q-264813": {
      "dom_id": "step-q264813",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{3}+{y}^{3}z,$ compute ${∇}_{x,z}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{x,z}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To compute ${∇}_{x,z}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $z$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{3}+{y}^{3}z) & ={y}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{y}^{3}+{y}^{3}z) & ={y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,z}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3} \\\\ {y}^{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
