    "q-264817": {
      "dom_id": "step-q264817",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{xy}{z},$ compute ${∇}_{y,z}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{y,z}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To compute ${∇}_{y,z}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $y$ and $z$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{xy}{z}) & =\\frac{x}{z} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{xy}{z}) & =-\\frac{xy}{{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{y,z}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{z} \\\\ -\\frac{xy}{{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
