      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{xyz},$ compute ${∇}_{x,y}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{x,y}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To compute ${∇}_{x,y}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $y$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xyz}) & =yz{e}^{xyz} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xyz}) & =xz{e}^{xyz}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,y}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}yz{e}^{xyz} \\\\ xz{e}^{xyz}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
