      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Given the function \n$f(x;w)={w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2},$\ncompute ${∇}_{w}\\,f$ with the input $x={[\\begin{aligned}5,\\,3\\end{aligned}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{w}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To compute ${∇}_{w}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to each component of $w.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})={x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, with $x={[\\begin{aligned}5,\\,3\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
