    "q-264884": {
      "dom_id": "step-q264884",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}$, compute ${∇}_{x,z}({∇}_{x,z}\\,f).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{x,z}({∇}_{x,z}f)=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "First, we take the variable subset gradient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,z}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ 2z\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives with respect to $x$ and $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x)=2\\,\\, &  & \\frac{∂}{∂z}(2x)=0 \\\\  & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2z)=0\\,\\, &  & \\frac{∂}{∂z}(2z)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,z}({∇}_{x,z}\\,f) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂z} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂z∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
