    "q-264888": {
      "dom_id": "step-q264888",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{yz}$, compute ${∇}_{x,y}({∇}_{x,y}\\,f).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{x,y}({∇}_{x,y}f)=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "First, we take the variable subset gradient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,y}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{yz}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{yz})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{yz} \\\\ xz{e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives with respect to $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{yz})=0\\,\\, &  & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{yz})=z{e}^{yz} \\\\  & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz{e}^{yz})=z{e}^{yz}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xz{e}^{yz})=x{z}^{2}{e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,y}({∇}_{x,y}\\,f) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & z{e}^{yz} \\\\ z{e}^{yz} & x{z}^{2}{e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
