    "q-263490": {
      "dom_id": "step-q263490",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x;w)=({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})^{2},$ compute ${∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f)=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$2{x}_{1}^{2}$</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute ${∇}_{w}\\,f$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})^{2}=2({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2}){x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})^{2}=2({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2}){x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}}=2{x}_{1}^{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}}=2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}}=2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}=2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}^{2} & 2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} & 2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
